        "text": "Pathway to NAD+: NMN — NMNAT (NMN adenylyltransferase — the enzyme that converts NMN to NAD+) enzymes (may convert to NR first). NR — NRK (nicotinamide riboside kinase — the enzyme that converts NR to NMN) pathway — enters cells directly, converts to NMN then NAD+. Efficacy (Human Data): NMN — Significantly raises whole-blood NAD+. NR — Significantly raises whole-blood NAD+. Head-to-Head: NMN — NMN and NR comparable — 2026 Nature Metabolism RCT (n=65). NR — NMN and NR comparable — same trial. Flush: NMN — None. NR — None. Cholesterol Effects: NMN — Not demonstrated. NR — Not demonstrated. Cellular Entry: NMN — Debated — may require conversion to NR first. NR — Direct cellular entry via transporters. Human Trial Volume: NMN — 20+ clinical studies. NR — 40+ clinical studies — more established. Regulatory Status: NMN — FDA reviewing as potential drug ingredient. NR — GRAS (Generally Recognized As Safe — FDA designation for established supplements) status — well-established supplement. Cost: NMN — [[REDACTED]]–150/month. NR — [[REDACTED]]–80/month. Best For: NMN — Those prioritizing convenience, no flush. NR — Best-studied NAD+ precursor, no flush."
