        "text": "Back to Peptide Library AOD-9604 Metabolic &amp; Weight Loss Research-Grade Last reviewed: May 23, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A modified fragment of the C-terminus of growth hormone (hGH 176-191), studied for fat loss without growth hormone&apos;s broader growth effects. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, usually morning; historically also studied orally Half-life ~30 minutes (subcutaneous) Typical research dose 250&ndash;500 mcg subcutaneously once daily, in 8&ndash;12 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved as a drug &mdash; research use only (holds limited GRAS food status). [[REDACTED]] What is AOD-9604? AOD-9604 &mdash; also written AOD9604 and known as Anti-Obesity Drug 9604, the hGH Fragment 176-191, or Tyr-hGH 177-191 &mdash; is a synthetic peptide fragment of human growth hormone, specifically the 16-amino-acid C-terminal sequence (amino acids 176-191) with a stabilizing tyrosine added at the front. It was developed in Australia in the 1990s to capture growth hormone&apos;s fat-burning effects without the broader hormonal side effects of full-length growth hormone. Despite six clinical trials in over 900 participants, it failed to demonstrate consistent weight loss in larger Phase 2b studies and was discontinued as a drug candidate in 2007. It remains available as a research peptide and has renewed interest for cartilage repair applications. New to peptide research? Start with the basics Reported benefits: Stimulates lipolysis (fat breakdown) without raising blood sugar or IGF-1 Modest weight reduction in early trials (2.6 kg vs 0.8 kg placebo over 12 weeks) Selective fat-mobilization without growth hormone&apos;s broader endocrine effects Well-tolerated safety profile across 900+ trial participants Investigational interest in cartilage repair and joint applications No measurable effect on insulin sensitivity or glucose homeostasis Common research dose: Historical clinical trials used oral doses of 0.25 mg, 0.5 mg, and 1.0 mg daily, plus subcutaneous formulations. Research-grade injectable AOD-9604 is typically dosed at 250–500 mcg subcutaneously once daily. Where to buy: PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides MOTS-c Cagrilintide Semaglutide Tirzepatide IGF-1 LR3 Related Blends AOD-9604 + MOTS-c Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
