        "text": "Back to Peptide Library BPC-157 Recovery &amp; Tissue Repair Research-Grade Last reviewed: May 23, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A lab-made 15-amino-acid peptide studied for wound healing, tendon and tissue repair, and gut protection. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, or oral for gut-related use Half-life Under 30 minutes (plasma) Typical research dose 250&ndash;500 mcg, once or twice daily, in 4&ndash;8 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. [[REDACTED]] What is BPC-157? BPC-157 is a 15-amino-acid synthetic peptide derived from a protective protein found in human gastric juice. It is also known as Body Protection Compound-157 (BPC 15, Pentadecapeptide BPC 157, PL 14736). Researchers have studied it for over 30 years for its remarkable wound healing, tendon repair, and gut protection effects in animal models. Despite 544+ published research articles between 1993 and 2024, no Phase 2 or Phase 3 human clinical trials have been completed. It remains one of the most popular research peptides for soft tissue recovery, with a notable safety profile and unusual stability across a wide pH range. Often paired with TB-500 as the Wolverine Stack for musculoskeletal recovery, or with GHK-Cu for combined connective-tissue repair. New to peptide research? Start with the basics Reported benefits: Accelerated tendon, ligament, and muscle healing in animal models (often 30–50% faster) Gastroprotection against NSAIDs, alcohol, and stress-induced ulcers Reduced systemic inflammation markers Stable across wide pH range (1–11), allowing oral and injectable delivery Improved peripheral nerve recovery in crush-injury models Reported reduction in pain and improved mobility within 5–10 days in user reports Common research dose: Most research protocols use 250–500 mcg subcutaneously once or twice daily. Typical cycle length is 4–8 weeks, sometimes extended to 12 weeks for chronic conditions. Oral formulations exist for gut-related research, though injectable produces stronger systemic effects. Where to buy: PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides TB-500 GHK-Cu KPV Thymosin Alpha-1 CJC-1295 Ipamorelin Related Blends GLOW KLOW KPV + BPC-157 Semaglutide + BPC-157 Tirzepatide + BPC-157 Wolverine Stack GH Stack Comparisons BPC-157 vs TB-500 BPC-157 vs GHK-Cu Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
