        "q": "How is GHRP-2 different from GHRP-6 and Ipamorelin?",
        "a": "All three activate the same ghrelin/GH-secretagogue receptor (GHSR-1a). The differences are potency and selectivity. GHRP-2 is a more potent GH releaser than GHRP-6 and produces less appetite stimulation, but it still raises cortisol, prolactin, and ACTH modestly. Ipamorelin is the most selective of the group &mdash; GH-only, with essentially no cortisol or prolactin effect. GHRP-2 sits in the middle: stronger GH release than ipamorelin, cleaner than GHRP-6."
