        "heading": "Page content",
        "text": "Back to Peptide Library GLOW Skin Health &amp; Anti-Aging Stack Last reviewed: May 15, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A fixed-dose combination of BPC-157, TB-500, and GHK-Cu &mdash; a 5:1:1 blend studied for skin quality, connective-tissue repair, and recovery in a single injection. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, 5 days on / 2 off, at bedtime (GHK-Cu is also used topically) Half-life Not established for the blend &mdash; varies by component Typical research dose 0.25&ndash;0.5 mL of the reconstituted 70 mg blend, 5 days/week, in 8&ndash;12 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. What is GLOW? GLOW is a research-grade 3-component peptide blend combining GHK-Cu (copper tripeptide), BPC-157 (gastric pentadecapeptide), and TB-500 (Thymosin Beta-4 fragment) in a single injection. The blend is designed to deliver complementary mechanisms — GHK-Cu drives collagen synthesis and gene expression modulation, BPC-157 promotes angiogenesis and tissue stabilization, and TB-500 enhances cellular migration and remodeling — through non-overlapping pathways. Common formulations use a 5:1:1 ratio (GHK-Cu:TB-500:BPC-157), often supplied as a 70 mg blend per vial: 50 mg GHK-Cu / 10 mg TB-500 / 10 mg BPC-157. For researchers needing an additional inflammation-control layer, the 4-component KLOW blend adds KPV on top of the GLOW backbone. Reported benefits: Comprehensive skin rejuvenation (collagen + elastin + tissue remodeling in one stack) Faster wound healing and reduced scarring Anti-inflammatory and antioxidant effects from three complementary mechanisms Hair follicle support Convenient single-injection format vs three separate peptide injections Synergistic effects from non-overlapping mechanisms Common research dose: Standard protocol: 0.25–0.5 mL of reconstituted blend, 5 days/week (5-on, 2-off), at bedtime. Approximately 40 doses per 70 mg vial. See Dosing &amp; Protocols below for details. Where to buy: GLOW is sold by specialty research peptide vendors as a compounded blend. None of the three component peptides are FDA-approved as injectables. See Verified Peptide Vendors for current options. Related supplements: Find related supplements on Amazon. [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides GHK-Cu BPC-157 TB-500 Related Blends Wolverine Stack KLOW Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
