        "text": "Back to Peptide Library KLOW Skin Health &amp; Anti-Aging Research-Grade Combination Blend Last reviewed: May 15, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A fixed-dose combination of BPC-157, TB-500, GHK-Cu, and KPV in a single injection &mdash; studied for tissue repair, skin remodeling, and anti-inflammatory/gut effects. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, once daily (commonly at bedtime) Half-life Not established for the blend &mdash; varies by component Typical research dose 0.1 mL (10 units) once daily from an 80 mg vial &mdash; ~2.5 mg GHK-Cu + 0.5 mg each BPC-157/TB-500/KPV &mdash; in 8&ndash;12 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. What is KLOW? KLOW is a research-grade 4-component peptide blend combining BPC-157 , TB-500 , GHK-Cu , and KPV in a single injection. It extends the 3-component GLOW blend by adding KPV, a tripeptide derived from α-melanocyte-stimulating hormone (α-MSH) that suppresses NF-κB-mediated inflammation. The result is the most comprehensive of the BPC/TB-based recovery blends: tissue repair from BPC-157 + TB-500, skin remodeling from GHK-Cu, and inflammation control from KPV — on a calmer tissue background. Reported benefits: Soft-tissue injury work with persistent inflammatory component (tendon, ligament, muscle) Post-procedure aesthetic recovery (microneedling, laser, surgery) Reactive or chronically inflamed skin where pure GLOW would aggravate Comprehensive collagen + extracellular matrix remodeling on top of inflammation suppression Gut and mucosal barrier work (mechanistic — based on KPV and BPC-157 component literature) Single-injection convenience vs four separate peptide protocols Common research dose: 0.1 mL (10 units on a U-100 insulin syringe) once daily subcutaneously from an 80 mg vial reconstituted with 2 mL bacteriostatic water — delivering ~2.5 mg GHK-Cu + 0.5 mg of each of BPC-157, TB-500, and KPV per dose. Standard cycle 8–12 weeks active, 4-week break. Where to buy: KLOW is sold by specialty research peptide vendors as a compounded blend, typically as an 80 mg vial. None of the four components are FDA-approved as injectables. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides BPC-157 TB-500 GHK-Cu KPV Related Blends Wolverine Stack GLOW Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
