        "text": "KPV and BPC-157 both act quickly on the molecular level. KPV’s NF-κB inhibition begins after the first dose; BPC-157’s cytoprotective signaling activates within days in animal models. Subjective improvements in gut symptoms typically appear in weeks 2–4 in research-community reports, with structural mucosal healing markers accumulating through weeks 4–8. In preclinical IBD and ulcer models, BPC-157 produces measurable mucosal protection within the first week of daily dosing. KPV’s cytokine-suppressing effect is similarly fast, with colonic inflammation scores improving across the first 1–2 weeks. For structural healing outcomes — ulcer resolution, tight-junction protein recovery, submucosal vasculature normalization — animal models show most improvement at 4–8 weeks. Standard research cycles run 6–8 weeks. An off period of 4 weeks is common before re-cycling. Some researchers run BPC-157 continuously for chronic GI applications and pulse KPV during active flare periods, though this is community-derived rather than protocol-validated."
