        "heading": "Page content",
        "text": "Back to Peptide Library KPV + BPC-157 Gut Healing &amp; IBD Anti-Inflammatory Research-Grade Combination Blend Last reviewed: May 28, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A fixed-dose research combination of KPV (an anti-inflammatory &alpha;-MSH tripeptide that blocks NF-&kappa;B signaling) and BPC-157 (a gut-protective recovery peptide), studied for gut/IBD, mucosal repair, and systemic inflammation. How it&apos;s taken Oral for gut-local action, or subcutaneous injection for systemic effects Half-life Not well characterized in humans for either component Typical research dose KPV 200&ndash;500 mcg/day + BPC-157 250&ndash;500 mcg/day, in 6&ndash;8 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. [[REDACTED]] What is the KPV + BPC-157 blend? KPV + BPC-157 is a research-grade 2-component peptide combination pairing KPV (lysine&ndash;proline&ndash;valine, the C-terminal tripeptide of &alpha;-MSH) with BPC-157 (Body Protection Compound, a stable gastric pentadecapeptide) for gut-healing and systemic anti-inflammatory research. KPV controls the inflammatory cascade by blocking NF-&kappa;B nuclear translocation intracellularly &mdash; suppressing TNF-&alpha;, IL-6, and IL-1&beta; production without engaging melanocortin receptors. BPC-157 simultaneously drives mucosal repair and angiogenesis through the nitric oxide / VEGFR2 / FAK-paxillin axis, restoring vascular integrity and tight-junction protein expression in damaged gut tissue. A key practical advantage of this pairing: both peptides can be dosed orally for gut-local effects, making it the most accessible combination for intestinal-mucosal research. Researchers wanting to add GHK-Cu and TB-500 for broader tissue repair and skin remodeling step up to KLOW &mdash; the 4-component blend that contains both KPV and BPC-157 at its core. Reported benefits: NF-&kappa;B-mediated inflammation suppression via intracellular KPV action (no melanocortin receptor involvement) Mucosal repair, ulcer healing, and gut barrier restoration via BPC-157 cytoprotection Pro-inflammatory cytokine suppression (TNF-&alpha;, IL-6, IL-1&beta;) alongside angiogenesis and VEGF upregulation Tight-junction protein restoration and submucosal vascular reconstruction Dual oral-route option: both peptides active via oral delivery for gut-local effects IBD and colitis model efficacy from both components independently Well-tolerated profile; KPV does not produce pigmentation or appetite changes Common research dose: KPV 200&ndash;500 mcg/day (oral or SC) + BPC-157 250&ndash;500 mcg/day (oral or SC). Both on empty stomach for oral administration. Cycle 6&ndash;8 weeks active, 4 weeks off. Where to buy: Sold as separate research-grade vials (KPV and BPC-157) by specialty peptide vendors; some vendors carry oral KPV capsules. Neither is FDA-approved. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides KPV BPC-157 GHK-Cu Thymosin Alpha-1 Related Blends KLOW Wolverine Stack Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
