        "text": "Back to Peptide Library LL-37 Gut Health &amp; Immunity Research-Grade Last reviewed: July 13, 2026 Quick Facts What it is The sole human cathelicidin-derived antimicrobial and host-defense peptide, studied for antimicrobial, wound-healing, and immune-modulating effects &mdash; with a genuinely double-edged inflammatory biology. How it&apos;s taken No validated human route or protocol &mdash; sold research-use-only Half-life Not well characterized in humans Typical research dose No validated human dose Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. [[REDACTED]] What is LL-37? LL-37 is the sole human cathelicidin antimicrobial peptide &mdash; a 37-amino-acid, positively charged, amphipathic peptide cleaved by proteases from the C-terminus of a precursor protein, hCAP18 (encoded by the CAMP gene); it also appears under the alias forms hCAP18/LL-37, the CAP-18 fragment, and LL37. Produced by neutrophils and epithelial cells at barrier surfaces such as skin, gut, and airway, it is a core component of innate immune defense, with broad-spectrum antimicrobial activity and a wide range of immunomodulatory effects including roles in wound healing, inflammation, and epithelial protection. Evidence honesty: LL-37 has a large, genuine basic-science literature &mdash; its mechanism and in-vitro antimicrobial activity are real and well cited. But two caveats define this profile: (1) in-vitro antimicrobial activity does not equal proven clinical efficacy &mdash; human therapeutic evidence is limited and LL-37 is not an approved treatment; and (2) its biology is double-edged &mdash; LL-37 is protective in host defense yet is also implicated in inflammatory conditions including psoriasis, rosacea, and lupus. It is not uniformly &ldquo;good.&rdquo; Research areas: Broad-spectrum antimicrobial activity against bacteria, fungi, and some viruses (largely in vitro) Wound healing and re-epithelialization at skin and mucosal surfaces Immunomodulation — chemotaxis, LPS neutralization, Toll-like-receptor modulation Epithelial and mucosal barrier defense (skin, gut, airway) Double-edged role: mechanistically implicated in psoriasis, rosacea, and lupus Dosing: There is no established, validated human therapeutic dose for LL-37. It is research-use-only, and the limited human literature does not support a standardized protocol. Where to buy: PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides KPV Thymosin Alpha-1 VIP Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
