        "text": "Back to Peptide Library MK-677 Performance &amp; Energy Research-Grade Last reviewed: May 23, 2026 Quick Facts What it is An orally active, lab-made ghrelin mimetic (GH secretagogue) that signals the pituitary to release the body&apos;s own growth hormone &mdash; studied for lean mass, recovery, sleep, and appetite. How it&apos;s taken Oral &mdash; capsule or liquid, once daily at bedtime Half-life ~24 hours Typical research dose 25 mg once daily (some start at 12.5 mg), in 8&ndash;16 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. WADA-prohibited (S2). [[REDACTED]] What is MK-677? MK-677 (ibutamoren) is an orally active, non-peptide ghrelin receptor agonist developed by Merck in the 1990s as a potential treatment for growth hormone deficiency, muscle wasting, and osteoporosis. It is also cataloged under the developmental codes MK-0677 and L-163,191, the salt form ibutamoren mesylate, and the later names LUM-201 and Oratrope. Despite Phase 2 trial data showing 24-hour sustained elevation of GH and IGF-1, MK-677 was never FDA-approved and remains an investigational compound. Unlike injectable GH secretagogues ( sermorelin , ipamorelin , tesamorelin ), MK-677 is taken orally &mdash; a major convenience advantage. It mimics ghrelin at the GHS-R1a receptor, triggering pulsatile GH release that preserves natural feedback loops, unlike exogenous GH injection which suppresses endogenous production. Note: MK-677 is technically NOT a peptide &mdash; it&apos;s a non-peptide small molecule ghrelin mimetic &mdash; but is included on Prof. Peptide because it acts on the same GH/IGF-1 axis as peptide secretagogues and is commonly compared to them. New to peptide research? Start with the basics Reported benefits: Sustained GH and IGF-1 elevation (24-hour duration per dose) Increased lean body mass without change in fat mass (1-year RCT data) Improved sleep quality (deeper slow-wave sleep) Increased appetite (useful for muscle gain, problematic for cutting) Oral administration &mdash; no injections Bone density improvement (1-year RCT) Common research dose: Standard research dose: 25 mg/day orally, taken at bedtime. This is the dose used in Merck&apos;s 1-year RCT in healthy older adults. Some users start at 12.5 mg/day for 1–2 weeks to assess tolerance. Where to buy: MK-677 is not FDA-approved and is sold as a research compound. PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides Ipamorelin CJC-1295 Sermorelin Tesamorelin IGF-1 LR3 Related Blends MK-677 + Ipamorelin Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
