        "text": "Back to Peptide Library MOTS-c Metabolic &amp; Weight Loss Research-Grade Last reviewed: May 23, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A peptide encoded inside the mitochondrial genome itself &mdash; a mitochondria-derived signal studied for insulin sensitivity, metabolism, muscle preservation, exercise capacity, and mitochondrial aging. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, once daily (morning, often pre-workout); a nasal-spray format is also sold Half-life Not well characterized in humans; dosed once daily by convention Typical research dose 5&ndash;10 mg subcutaneously once daily, in 4&ndash;12 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. Phase 1 trials begun. [[REDACTED]] What is MOTS-c? MOTS-c (short for Mitochondrial ORF of the 12S rRNA Type-c, sometimes written MOTSc) is a 16-amino-acid peptide encoded inside the mitochondrial genome itself &mdash; making it one of the first known mitochondria-derived peptides. Classed as a Mitochondrial-Derived Peptide (MDP) and often described as an AMPK activator or exercise mimetic. Discovered in 2015 at USC, it acts as a hormone-like signal from mitochondria to the rest of the body, regulating metabolism through AMPK pathways (the same master energy regulator activated by metformin and exercise). Research interest has focused on insulin resistance, type 2 diabetes, muscle preservation, and cellular aging. MOTS-c blood levels naturally decline with age, which has made it a candidate for longevity research. New to peptide research? Start with the basics Reported benefits: Improved insulin sensitivity and glucose uptake in skeletal muscle (preclinical) AMPK pathway activation similar to metformin and exercise Reduced muscle wasting through suppression of myostatin signaling Cardiovascular protection in diabetic models Potential anti-aging effects through mitochondrial function support Common research dose: MOTS-c is in early-stage clinical research. Animal studies use 0.5–15 mg/kg/day. Common research-grade human dose is 5–10 mg subcutaneously once daily, though there is no validated clinical dosing standard. Where to buy: PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides Cagrilintide AOD-9604 NAD+ Epitalon Semaglutide Related Blends NAD+ + MOTS-c + 5-Amino-1MQ AOD-9604 + MOTS-c Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
