        "heading": "Page content",
        "text": "Back to Peptide Library Metabolic Blend (NAD+ + MOTS-c + 5-Amino-1MQ) Metabolic &amp; Longevity Research-Grade Combination Blend Last reviewed: May 29, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A combination of NAD+ (an energy-metabolism coenzyme), MOTS-c (a mitochondrial-derived metabolic peptide), and 5-Amino-1MQ (a small-molecule NNMT inhibitor), stacked for metabolism and longevity. How it&apos;s taken Mixed route &mdash; NAD+ subcutaneous or IV, MOTS-c subcutaneous injection, 5-Amino-1MQ oral (or dissolved into the combined vial for SC) Half-life Varies by component; not characterized for the combination Typical research dose NAD+ 50&ndash;100 mg SC daily + MOTS-c 5&ndash;10 mg/week SC + 5-Amino-1MQ ~50 mg/day oral; 4&ndash;8 week cycles Research status None FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. [[REDACTED]] What is NAD+ + MOTS-c + 5-Amino-1MQ? The Metabolic Blend is a research-grade 3-component formulation combining NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide), MOTS-c (a mitochondrial-derived peptide), and 5-Amino-1MQ (a small-molecule NNMT inhibitor) in a single lyophilized vial. All three converge on the same metabolic axis &mdash; mitochondrial energy production and the NAD+ signaling network that powers cellular longevity, metabolic flexibility, and fat metabolism. NAD+ replenishes the coenzyme substrate that declines with age; MOTS-c activates AMPK to improve how cells use that substrate; 5-Amino-1MQ blocks a major NAD+ precursor consumption pathway to raise the steady-state intracellular NAD+ pool. It is a vendor- and community-formulated product with no controlled clinical trial as a combination. Reported benefits: Mitochondrial NAD+ replenishment and sirtuin/PARP activation via direct NAD+ delivery AMPK-mediated metabolic flexibility, insulin sensitivity, and exercise-mimetic signaling via MOTS-c Raised intracellular NAD+ and SAM via NNMT inhibition (5-Amino-1MQ) Adipocyte fat-metabolism modulation and body-composition effects (preclinical evidence only for 5-Amino-1MQ) Mitochondrial biogenesis support via convergent AMPK/PGC-1α and SIRT1 signaling Age-related muscle homeostasis and physical performance preservation (preclinical MOTS-c data) Common research dose: NAD+ 50&ndash;100 mg SC once daily + MOTS-c 5&ndash;10 mg/week SC (split daily or alternate-day) + 5-Amino-1MQ ~50 mg/day (oral as standalone, or per vial ratio if combined SC). Combined vial products vary by vendor &mdash; verify per-component breakdown on Certificate of Analysis. Where to buy: The three components (NAD+, MOTS-c, 5-Amino-1MQ) are sold by specialty research peptide vendors; our data does not confirm a pre-blended vial. None of the three components are FDA-approved as injectables. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides NAD+ MOTS-c Epitalon Related Blends Semaglutide + BPC-157 Tirzepatide + BPC-157 Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
