        "text": "Back to Peptide Library PDA (Pentadeca Arginate) Recovery &amp; Tissue Repair Research-Grade Last reviewed: July 13, 2026 Quick Facts What it is Pentadeca Arginate &mdash; a synthetic 15-amino-acid, arginate-stabilized peptide that is the salt-form variant of BPC-157 (same sequence), studied for tissue repair and recovery. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, once or twice daily Half-life Not characterized in humans Typical research dose 250&ndash;500 mcg subcutaneously, once or twice daily, in 4&ndash;8 week cycles (extrapolated from BPC-157) Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. Inherits BPC-157&apos;s FDA Category 2 status (Nov 2023). [[REDACTED]] What is PDA (Pentadeca Arginate)? Pentadeca Arginate (PDA) is the arginate-salt form of BPC-157 &mdash; the same 15-amino-acid synthetic peptide (sequence GEPPPGKPADDAGLV), supplied with an arginine counterion instead of the acetate counterion used in conventional BPC-157. In plain terms, PDA is essentially a salt-form variant of BPC-157: the peptide that reaches tissue is the same molecule, so PDA has no independent research base of its own. It is marketed as a more stable, upgraded version, but as of 2026 no peer-reviewed study has investigated PDA as a distinct compound. Evidence honesty: The widely-repeated claim that PDA is &ldquo;1,000× more stable than BPC-157 acetate&rdquo; is unpublished vendor marketing, not a peer-reviewed finding &mdash; there is no head-to-head study behind it. Every mechanistic and tissue-repair claim for PDA is extrapolated from the BPC-157 literature, which is itself almost entirely preclinical. Treat PDA as a salt-form variant of BPC-157, and evaluate it on the (preclinical) BPC-157 evidence base. What is genuinely known: PDA is the arginate salt of the same peptide as BPC-157 &mdash; identical amino-acid sequence Its proposed mechanisms (angiogenesis, growth-factor and collagen support, tendon-to-bone signaling) are BPC-157&apos;s, demonstrated in animal models No peer-reviewed study has investigated PDA specifically; a 2025 systematic review of BPC-157 found only one small human study The &ldquo;1,000× stability&rdquo; and &ldquo;upgraded BPC-157&rdquo; claims are unverified vendor marketing It inherits BPC-157&apos;s FDA Category 2 status (Nov 2023) and is sold research-use-only Common research dose: Extrapolated from BPC-157 protocols &mdash; typically 250–500 mcg subcutaneously once or twice daily in 4–8 week cycles. No PDA-specific pharmacokinetic data exists. Where to buy: PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides TB-500 GHK-Cu KPV Wolverine Stack Compare See the full BPC-157 profile Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
