        "heading": "Page content",
        "text": "Back to Peptide Library Retatrutide Metabolic &amp; Weight Loss Investigational Last reviewed: May 17, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A lab-made peptide that activates three metabolic hormone receptors at once &mdash; GLP-1, GIP, and glucagon &mdash; studied for weight loss and obesity. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, once weekly Half-life ~6 days Typical research dose Starts at 2 mg once weekly, escalating every 4 weeks toward a 12 mg maintenance dose Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; investigational (Phase 3); research use only. [[REDACTED]] Latest research: Phase 3 TRIUMPH-1 results released May 21, 2026 &mdash; 30.3% average weight loss at 104 weeks, comparable to bariatric surgery outcomes. Read the full breakdown What is Retatrutide? Retatrutide (LY3437943) is a once-weekly injectable peptide developed by Eli Lilly that activates three different hormone receptors at once: GLP-1, GIP, and glucagon. The first two are the receptors targeted by existing weight-loss drugs &mdash; Semaglutide (Ozempic, Wegovy) hits GLP-1; Tirzepatide (Mounjaro, Zepbound) hits both GLP-1 and GIP &mdash; but retatrutide adds a third, glucagon, which boosts resting energy expenditure on top of the appetite-suppression effects shared across the class. That third receptor is the reason retatrutide has produced the largest weight losses ever recorded in a pharmacological trial: roughly 24% of body weight at 48 weeks in Phase 2 obesity research, with the weight-loss curve still declining at trial end. As of mid-2026, the drug is in Phase 3 trials under Eli Lilly&rsquo;s TRIUMPH program, with regulatory submission targeted for late 2026 and potential approval in 2027 or 2028. Reported benefits: Significant body weight reduction in Phase 2 obesity trials (averaging ~24% at 48 weeks at the highest dose) Improved glycemic control in Phase 2 type 2 diabetes trials (HbA1c reductions around 2.2%) Appetite suppression and reduced food intake Improvements in liver fat markers in early MASLD substudy data Improvements in blood pressure and lipid profiles alongside weight loss Once-weekly dosing (half-life around 6 days) Common research dose: Published Phase 2 protocols ranged from 2 mg to 12 mg subcutaneously once weekly, with the highest weight-loss figures observed at the 12 mg dose. Protocols followed in research and user communities draw from these published dose escalations and from animal research, not from finalized human clinical guidelines. Where to buy: PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides Tirzepatide Semaglutide Cagrilintide CagriSema MK-677 Related Blends Wolverine Stack GH Stack GLOW KLOW Comparisons Retatrutide vs Tirzepatide Retatrutide vs Semaglutide Semaglutide vs Tirzepatide vs Retatrutide Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
