        "text": "Back to Peptide Library Semaglutide Metabolic &amp; Weight Loss FDA-Approved Last reviewed: May 18, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A lab-made peptide that mimics GLP-1, a gut hormone released after eating &mdash; it curbs appetite and slows stomach emptying, and is the most-studied GLP-1 medication, used for type 2 diabetes, weight management, and cardiovascular risk reduction. How it&apos;s taken Once-weekly subcutaneous injection; also available as a daily oral tablet (Rybelsus, type 2 diabetes only) Half-life ~165 hours (~7 days) Typical research dose 0.25 mg once weekly, escalating every 4 weeks (0.25 &rarr; 2.4 mg) to a 2.4 mg maintenance dose Research status FDA-approved (Ozempic, Wegovy, Rybelsus); research-grade sold for lab use only. [[REDACTED]] What is Semaglutide? Semaglutide is an FDA-approved peptide that mimics GLP-1, a hormone the gut releases after eating, to slow stomach emptying, suppress appetite, and improve insulin response. It is the active ingredient in three branded medications &mdash; Ozempic (type 2 diabetes, approved 2017), Wegovy (chronic weight management, approved 2021), and Rybelsus (oral type 2 diabetes, approved 2019). With eight-plus years of clinical use and seven FDA-approved indications, it has the longest safety record and largest body of clinical evidence of any GLP-class medication. Sibling compounds tirzepatide (dual GLP-1/GIP) and retatrutide (triple GLP-1/GIP/glucagon) build on the same receptor pathway with additional targets. New to peptide research? Start with the basics Reported benefits: Average 14.9% body weight loss over 68 weeks at the 2.4 mg dose (STEP 1 trial) 20% reduction in major adverse cardiovascular events in adults with obesity and established heart disease (SELECT trial) Lower blood sugar and A1C in type 2 diabetes (1–2% reduction) Reduced appetite and slower stomach emptying Slowed progression of kidney disease in users with diabetes 73% reduction in new diabetes diagnoses in SELECT participants without diabetes at baseline Once-weekly dosing (half-life around 7 days) Common research dose: FDA-approved dosing for weight management starts at 0.25 mg once weekly and escalates every 4 weeks (0.25 → 0.5 → 1.0 → 1.7 → 2.4 mg) up to a maximum of 2.4 mg weekly. For type 2 diabetes (Ozempic), maximum dose is 2.0 mg weekly. Research-grade dosing protocols mirror the approved schedule. Where to buy: Brand-name Ozempic, Wegovy, and Rybelsus require a prescription. Research-grade semaglutide is sold by specialty peptide vendors for laboratory use only. PP maintains a vetted list of vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides Tirzepatide Retatrutide Cagrilintide CagriSema Related Blends Semaglutide + BPC-157 Comparisons Retatrutide vs Semaglutide Semaglutide vs Tirzepatide Semaglutide vs Tirzepatide vs Retatrutide Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
