        "heading": "Page content",
        "text": "Back to Peptide Library Semax + Selank Cognitive &amp; Nootropic Research-Grade Combination Blend Last reviewed: May 15, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A combination of Semax (a nootropic/neuroprotective ACTH(4-10) peptide) and Selank (an anxiolytic tuftsin-derived peptide), stacked in a single intranasal spray for focus, mood, and stress. How it&apos;s taken Intranasal spray (nose-to-brain), typically in the morning; subcutaneous is possible but less common Half-life Very short for both components (minutes in plasma), but CNS effects last hours Typical research dose 1&ndash;3 sprays per nostril, 1&ndash;3&times; daily (~100 mcg of each peptide per spray), in 2&ndash;6 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only (both components approved as pharmaceuticals in Russia). What is Semax + Selank? Semax + Selank is a 2-component intranasal peptide blend pairing two synthetic heptapeptides: Semax (an ACTH(4-10) analog) and Selank (a tuftsin analog). Both were developed at the Institute of Molecular Genetics of the Russian Academy of Sciences and are approved as pharmaceuticals in Russia — Semax for post-stroke neuroprotection and cognitive applications, Selank for generalized anxiety disorder. The blend pairs cognitive enhancement (Semax: BDNF upregulation, dopaminergic and serotonergic modulation) with anxiolytic effects (Selank: indirect GABAergic modulation) in a single intranasal spray — producing sharper focus and reduced anxiety simultaneously, without sedation, dependence, or withdrawal. Reported benefits: Cognitive performance under stress (Semax cognitive effects + Selank anxiety reduction) Anxiolytic effect without sedation, dependence, or withdrawal (Selank advantage over benzodiazepines) BDNF upregulation supporting memory consolidation and neuroplasticity Post-stroke neuroprotection (Semax approved Russian clinical indication) Mood and motivation effects through dopaminergic and serotonergic modulation Intranasal delivery — rapid CNS effect, bypasses first-pass hepatic metabolism Common research dose: 1–3 sprays per nostril, 1–3× daily — typically ~100 mcg of each peptide per spray when a 20 mg vial (10 mg + 10 mg) is reconstituted into a 10 mL nasal spray bottle. Standard total daily dose: 300–600 mcg Semax + 300–900 mcg Selank, consistent with the per-component Russian clinical protocols. Where to buy: Semax and Selank are sold by specialty research peptide vendors; a combined preparation, where used, is typically reconstituted into a nasal spray. Neither component is FDA-approved (both are approved in Russia). See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides Semax Selank DSIP Epitalon Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
