        "text": "Back to Peptide Library Sermorelin Growth Hormone Research-Grade Last reviewed: May 23, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A lab-made copy of the body&apos;s own GHRH signal &mdash; the 29-amino-acid fragment that prompts the pituitary to release its own growth hormone, studied for recovery, lean mass, and sleep. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, once daily at bedtime Half-life ~10&ndash;20 minutes Typical research dose 200&ndash;500 mcg once daily at bedtime, in 3&ndash;6 month cycles Research status Formerly FDA-approved as Geref (discontinued 2008) &mdash; now research use only. [[REDACTED]] What is Sermorelin? Sermorelin is a synthetic 29-amino-acid analog of growth hormone-releasing hormone (GHRH) &mdash; specifically the first 29 amino acids of native GHRH, which contain the entire biological activity of the parent hormone. Also known by the shorthand GRF (1-29) or GHRH(1-29)-NH2, it was originally developed by Serono and FDA-approved as Geref in 1990 for diagnosis of growth hormone deficiency in children. The brand was discontinued in 2008 (not for safety or efficacy reasons), but sermorelin remains widely used in compounding pharmacy and research-grade contexts. It stimulates pulsatile GH release through GHRH receptor activation, with a short half-life (~10–20 minutes) requiring frequent dosing. Often paired with ipamorelin for dual-pathway GH amplification, conceptually similar to the GH Stack (which uses CJC-1295 in place of sermorelin). New to peptide research? Start with the basics Reported benefits: Stimulates natural pulsatile growth hormone release via GHRH receptor Increases IGF-1 through GH-mediated pathway Supports lean muscle growth, fat reduction, recovery (downstream of GH) Improved sleep quality reported with bedtime dosing Bone density support in clinical research Generally cleaner safety profile than other GHRH analogs (was FDA-approved) Common research dose: Most research protocols use 200–500 mcg subcutaneously once daily, typically at bedtime. Cycle length is typically 3–6 months for adult GHRH-replacement protocols. Empty-stomach dosing required for full GH response. Where to buy: PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides CJC-1295 Ipamorelin Tesamorelin MK-677 IGF-1 LR3 Related Blends Sermorelin + Ipamorelin GH Stack Wolverine Stack Comparisons CJC-1295 vs Sermorelin vs Ipamorelin Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
