        "heading": "Page content",
        "text": "Back to Peptide Library TB-500 Recovery &amp; Tissue Repair Research-Grade Last reviewed: May 23, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A lab-made fragment of a natural repair protein (Thymosin Beta-4), studied for wound healing, muscle and tendon recovery, and cardiac and corneal repair. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, once or twice weekly Half-life Multiple days (estimated from animal studies) Typical research dose 2.0&ndash;2.5 mg twice weekly to load, then ~2.0 mg weekly; 6&ndash;8 week cycles Research status Not FDA-approved &mdash; research use only. [[REDACTED]] What is TB-500? TB-500 is a synthetic fragment of Thymosin Beta-4 (Tβ4), a naturally occurring 43-amino-acid peptide found in virtually all mammalian cells. TB-500 corresponds to the active Tβ4 17-23 region of Thymosin Beta-4 (gene symbol TMSB4X). Unlike the full Thymosin Beta-4 protein, TB-500 is a shorter active fragment that&apos;s easier to synthesize and study. Researchers have studied it for over two decades, primarily for wound healing, cardiac repair, and corneal regeneration. It&apos;s commonly paired with BPC-157 in tissue-repair research protocols (the Wolverine Stack ). New to peptide research? Start with the basics Reported benefits: Accelerated wound healing in dermal, corneal, and cardiac tissue (animal models) Promotes new blood vessel formation (angiogenesis) Reduces fibrosis and scarring during repair Anti-inflammatory effects through NF-κB pathway modulation Mobilizes stem and progenitor cells to injury sites Pairs synergistically with BPC-157 in musculoskeletal repair research Common research dose: Most research protocols use 2.0–2.5 mg subcutaneously twice weekly for the first 4 weeks (loading phase), then 2.0 mg once weekly for maintenance. Total cycle length is typically 6–8 weeks, followed by 4–6 weeks off. Where to buy: PP maintains a vetted list of peptide vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides BPC-157 GHK-Cu KPV Thymosin Alpha-1 MK-677 Related Blends GLOW KLOW Wolverine Stack Comparisons BPC-157 vs TB-500 Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
