        "text": "Tirzepatide is administered as a once-weekly subcutaneous injection. The FDA-approved titration schedule starts at 2.5 mg and increases every 4 weeks through six dose tiers (2.5 → 5 → 7.5 → 10 → 12.5 → 15 mg) over 20 weeks. Maintenance doses are 5, 10, or 15 mg weekly depending on tolerance and goals. The approved labels titrate rather than start at a maintenance dose; faster escalation significantly increases GI side effects without improving outcomes. FDA-approved escalation schedule (SURMOUNT-1 protocol): Weeks 1–4. 2.5 mg once weekly (initiation dose, not for chronic use). Weeks 5–8. 5 mg once weekly. Weeks 9–12. 7.5 mg once weekly. Weeks 13–16. 10 mg once weekly. Weeks 17–20. 12.5 mg once weekly. Weeks 21+. 15 mg once weekly (maximum dose). Maintenance doses are 5, 10, or 15 mg weekly. Most users continue increasing through the schedule until they reach their target weight loss or hit dose-limiting side effects. The Mounjaro label increases the dose only after at least 4 weeks on the current one, so remaining at a step longer is within the labelled schedule, and the published outcomes do not show that extension reducing long-term outcomes. Half-life is approximately 5 days (~120 hours), supporting once-weekly dosing with steady state reached in roughly 4 weeks at each dose level. Dose adjustments aren&rsquo;t typically needed for kidney or liver impairment, though dehydration from GI side effects can affect kidney function and should be monitored. For research-grade tirzepatide outside FDA-approved use, dosing protocols mirror the approved schedule. There are no separate research-grade dosing standards. Need to calculate your dose? Convert mg to syringe units and plan reconstitution with the dosage calculator . Common question: How often is tirzepatide dosed?"
