        "heading": "Page content",
        "text": "Back to Peptide Library Tirzepatide Metabolic &amp; Weight Loss FDA-Approved Last reviewed: May 18, 2026 Quick Facts What it is A lab-made peptide that activates two gut-hormone receptors at once &mdash; GIP and GLP-1 &mdash; the first dual incretin agonist, studied for weight loss and type 2 diabetes. How it&apos;s taken Subcutaneous injection, once weekly Half-life ~5 days (~120 hours) Typical research dose Titrated from 2.5 mg, increasing every 4 weeks (2.5&rarr;5&rarr;7.5&rarr;10&rarr;12.5&rarr;15 mg) to a 15 mg weekly maximum Research status FDA-approved as Mounjaro and Zepbound &mdash; research-grade sold for laboratory use only. [[REDACTED]] What is Tirzepatide? Tirzepatide (LY3298176) is an FDA-approved peptide that activates two metabolic receptors at once &mdash; GLP-1 and GIP &mdash; making it the first dual incretin agonist on market. It is the active ingredient in two branded medications: Mounjaro (type 2 diabetes, approved May 2022) and Zepbound (chronic weight management, approved November 2023; obstructive sleep apnea expansion December 2024). Unlike older GLP-1 drugs like semaglutide that target one receptor, tirzepatide&rsquo;s dual mechanism produced significantly more weight loss in head-to-head SURMOUNT-5 (20.2% vs 13.7% over 72 weeks). Retatrutide extends the same architecture with a third receptor (glucagon) and is in Phase 3 trials. New to peptide research? Start with the basics Reported benefits: Significant weight loss (average 20.2% over 72 weeks at max dose in SURMOUNT-5) Lower blood sugar and A1C in type 2 diabetes (2.0–2.5% reduction) Reduced appetite and slower stomach emptying Improvements in cholesterol and blood pressure Better insulin sensitivity Reduced obstructive sleep apnea severity (SURMOUNT-OSA) Once-weekly dosing (half-life around 5 days) Common research dose: FDA-approved dosing starts at 2.5 mg once weekly by subcutaneous injection, then increases every 4 weeks (2.5 → 5 → 7.5 → 10 → 12.5 → 15 mg) up to a maximum of 15 mg weekly. Most users settle at maintenance doses between 10 mg and 15 mg. Research-grade dosing protocols mirror the approved schedule. Where to buy: Brand-name Mounjaro and Zepbound require a prescription. Research-grade tirzepatide is sold by specialty peptide vendors for laboratory use only. PP maintains a vetted list of vendors with verified discount codes. See Verified Discount Codes for current options. [[REDACTED]] [[REDACTED]] Related Peptides Retatrutide Semaglutide Cagrilintide CagriSema Related Blends Tirzepatide + BPC-157 Comparisons Retatrutide vs Tirzepatide Semaglutide vs Tirzepatide Semaglutide vs Tirzepatide vs Retatrutide Need to calculate a dose? Use the Prof. Peptide dosage calculator for accurate reconstitution and dosing math. Open Calculator"
