        "text": "Back to Supplement Library Alpha-GPC Cognitive &amp; Nootropic Last reviewed: May 24, 2026 Also Known As: Alpha-glycerophosphocholine, L-alpha glycerylphosphorylcholine, choline alfoscerate, Gliatilin (Italian Rx brand) Supplement Class: Choline-containing phospholipid / acetylcholine precursor Evidence Tier: Strong — multiple Italian RCTs in dementia (prescription in Italy as Gliatilin), Ziegenfuss 2008 GH/exercise RCT, multiple healthy-user reaction-time and force-production RCTs What is Alpha-GPC? Alpha-GPC (alpha-glycerophosphocholine) is the most bioavailable, brain-penetrant choline source available as a supplement. It outperforms choline bitartrate and CDP-choline for raising plasma and brain choline — the substrate the brain needs to synthesize acetylcholine, the neurotransmitter central to attention, memory, and learning. Approximately 90% of adults don&apos;t consume adequate dietary choline, so the supplement bridges a real nutritional gap. In Italy, Alpha-GPC is sold as a prescription drug (Gliatilin) for cognitive impairment and dementia; in the rest of the world, it&apos;s available over-the-counter and widely used in nootropic stacks. The biohacker case is built on three things: a substantial dementia RCT base, acute exercise GH and force-production evidence, and a strong mechanistic rationale for stacking with cognitive peptides that work via different pathways. Reported benefits: Most effective choline source for raising brain acetylcholine Improved attention, reaction time, and working memory in healthy users (RCT evidence) Significant cognitive improvements in Alzheimer&apos;s-type and vascular dementia at clinical doses Acute growth hormone release (+44% peak) coupled to resistance exercise Enhanced lower-body force production at pre-workout doses Neuronal membrane support via phosphatidylcholine precursor pathway Substrate for racetam stacks (piracetam, aniracetam, oxiracetam) Common dose: 300–600 mg once daily for cognitive baseline; 600 mg taken 60–90 minutes pre-workout for the acute GH and force-production effect; 1200 mg/day in divided doses for clinical dementia research (not a healthy-user starting point). Where to buy: Available over-the-counter from most supplement retailers. Quality varies — review the quality-markers checklist in the Where to Buy section below before purchasing. [[REDACTED]] Related Supplements Lion&apos;s Mane Bacopa Monnieri Phosphatidylserine L-Theanine"
