        "heading": "Page content",
        "text": "Back to Supplement Library Caffeine + L-Theanine Cognitive &amp; Nootropic Performance &amp; Energy Last reviewed: May 24, 2026 Also Known As: Smart caffeine, the focus stack, caffeine+theanine, &ldquo;tea-like&rdquo; stack Supplement Class: Stimulant + amino acid stack (adenosine receptor antagonist + alpha-wave / GABA modulator) Component supplements: Caffeine + L-Theanine (canonical 1:2 ratio, ~100 mg caffeine + 200 mg L-theanine) Evidence Tier: Strong — multiple double-blind crossover RCTs (Owen 2008, Haskell 2008, Giesbrecht 2010, Einother 2010) independently replicate the synergy on attention switching, executive control, reaction time, and anxiety mitigation; meta-analysis support (Camfield 2014) What is the Caffeine + L-Theanine stack? Caffeine + L-Theanine is one of the most extensively researched cognitive supplement stacks in existence — and one of the few where the synergy between two compounds is demonstrably better than either compound alone in published RCTs. Caffeine is the world&apos;s most-used psychoactive compound, an adenosine receptor antagonist that drives alertness, faster reaction times, and reduced perception of fatigue. L-theanine is an amino acid found almost exclusively in tea leaves (Camellia sinensis) that promotes alpha-wave activity and modulates GABA, producing calm focus without sedation. Combined at the canonical 1:2 ratio (~100 mg caffeine + 200 mg L-theanine), they produce the alertness and executive-control benefit of caffeine, minus most of its anxiety, jitter, and cardiovascular edge. This is the neurochemical reason tea feels calmer than coffee — and the protocol most biohackers settle on once they&apos;ve experimented past coffee alone. Reported benefits: Focused alertness without the jitter, anxiety, or BP bump of caffeine alone (RCT-documented) Significantly improved attention switching and executive control vs caffeine alone (Owen 2008, Einother 2010) Faster reaction times and better word recognition under cognitive load (Haskell 2008) Sustained focus through demanding tasks (3–4+ hours of clean window) Smoother &ldquo;caffeine taper&rdquo; on the back end — less crash Reduced caffeine-induced anxiety and subjective tension (significant in multiple RCTs) Compatible with daily use; ratio adjustable for individual caffeine tolerance Common dose: Canonical 1:2 ratio — 100 mg caffeine + 200 mg L-theanine — taken 30–60 minutes before sustained-attention tasks. The published dose range spans 1:1 to 1:4; the 1:2 protocol is the most-replicated. Light starting dose: 50 mg caffeine + 100 mg L-theanine. High-tolerance: 200 mg caffeine + 400 mg L-theanine. Where to buy: Available over-the-counter as combined capsules or separate caffeine tablets + L-theanine capsules. Quality varies — review the quality-markers checklist in the Where to Buy section below before purchasing. [[REDACTED]] Related Supplements Caffeine L-Theanine Alpha-GPC Lion&apos;s Mane Bacopa Monnieri Rhodiola Rosea"
