        "heading": "What does resveratrol stack with?",
        "text": "Resveratrol pairs naturally with the longevity / NAD+ / sirtuin pathway toolkit. The SIRT1-activation mechanism complements NAD+ substrate supply, autophagy inducers, senolytics, and other longevity supplements. The Sinclair-protocol NMN + resveratrol pairing is the canonical longevity-stack combination. The three areas below cover the natural stacking categories. With peptides Resveratrol pairs naturally with the longevity peptide cluster — particularly via the NAD+ / sirtuin axis. NAD+ peptide (injectable / subcutaneous) delivers NAD+ directly into circulation, bypassing oral bioavailability constraints. Resveratrol activates sirtuins; NAD+ peptide supplies the substrate sirtuins require to function. The two operate on different layers of the same pathway and are mechanistically complementary. Epitalon adds the pineal-axis longevity arm — telomere maintenance and circadian regulation through a separate pathway. The three-peptide longevity stack (NAD+ peptide + Epitalon + resveratrol + NMN) covers SIRT1 activation, NAD+ substrate (oral + injectable routes), and pineal-axis regulation. Mechanistically coherent, no known negative interactions. The combination trial evidence is thinner than for individual components. With supplements NMN — the canonical Sinclair-protocol pairing. NMN supplies NAD+ substrate; resveratrol activates the sirtuins that use it. Trial evidence for the combination is thinner than for individual components, but the mechanistic rationale is mature. Oral NAD+ supplements — alternative NAD+ precursor stack. Same logic as NMN pairing. Spermidine — autophagy activator via EP300 inhibition. Different aging-biology arm; common longevity-stack co-occupant. Quercetin — senolytic flavonoid. Compatible longevity-stack co-occupant; mechanistically complementary (senolytic clearance + sirtuin activation). Apigenin — CD38 inhibitor preserving NAD+. Mechanism complement to resveratrol&apos;s sirtuin activation by reducing NAD+ consumption. CoQ10 — mitochondrial electron carrier and antioxidant. Compatible cardiovascular and mitochondrial pairing. Pterostilbene — methylated resveratrol analog with better bioavailability. Reasonable to stack both compounds for complementary kinetics via the same pathway. With lifestyle Take with fat-containing meals. Bioavailability is meaningfully fat-dependent. Pair with dietary fat (nuts, olive oil, fatty fish, avocado). Intermittent fasting. Caloric restriction and IF activate SIRT1 independently. Resveratrol may add modest mimetic effect during fasting windows. Mechanistically reasonable; not directly RCT-validated as combination. Exercise. Endurance exercise activates AMPK and SIRT1; resveratrol may have additive effect. Some animal data suggests resveratrol mimics exercise effects in sedentary populations but may blunt exercise-induced adaptations in active populations. Mediterranean diet. Resveratrol works on top of dietary polyphenol intake. The original French Paradox observation was about red wine in the context of Mediterranean diet — diet matters more than supplementation. Track biomarkers, not subjective effects. Resveratrol effects are biomarker-grade — track BP, HbA1c, lipid panel, inflammatory markers (CRP). Don&apos;t expect to &ldquo;feel&rdquo; resveratrol working."
